{"availability":"available","full":"tus/tusd","name":"tusd","description":"Reference server implementation in Go of tus: the open protocol for resumable file uploads","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":3892,"forks":555,"created":"2013-03-16T20:40:08Z","updated":"2026-10-07T07:18:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tus.github.io/tusd","topics":[],"demo":"https://tus.github.io/tusd","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.268Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.268Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.268Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.268Z","stars":3892,"forks":555}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["tus is a protocol based on HTTP for resumable file uploads. Resumable means that an upload can be interrupted at any moment and can be resumed without re-uploading the previous data again. An interruption may happen willingly, if the user wants to pause, or by accident in case of a network issue or server outage.","tusd is the official reference implementation of the tus resumable upload protocol. The protocol specifies a flexible method to upload files to remote servers using HTTP. The special feature is the ability to pause and resume uploads at any moment allowing to continue seamlessly after e.g. network interruptions.","It is capable of accepting uploads with arbitrary sizes and storing them locally on disk, on Google Cloud Storage or on AWS S3 (or any other S3-compatible storage system). Due to its modularization and extensibility, support for nearly any other cloud provider could easily be added to tusd."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tus/tusd/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0e5dc59922713efbee072b052727ccb613f3cefbf35fcbb8a2edba152a17c2d5","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.316Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.316Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"tus is a protocol based on HTTP for resumable file uploads. Resumable means that an upload can be interrupted at any moment and can be resumed without re-uploading the previous data again. An interruption may happen willingly, if the user wants to pause, or by accident in case of a network issue or server outage.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tus/tusd/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0e5dc59922713efbee072b052727ccb613f3cefbf35fcbb8a2edba152a17c2d5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tus/tusd/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.316Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T07:18:00Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tus/tusd/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:54.317Z","hash":"0e5dc59922713efbee072b052727ccb613f3cefbf35fcbb8a2edba152a17c2d5","originalBytes":1988,"storedBytes":1988,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tusd","any","protocol","resumable","upload","uploads","after","cloud","documentation","license","moment","network","other","pause","previous","release","storage","tus","using","ability","accepting","accident","added","again.","allowing","arbitrary","aws","based","been","branch","breaking","build","capable","case","changes","configuring","contains","continue","continuous-integration","could","data","disk","due","e.g.","easily","entire","extensibility","feature","file","files","flexible","found","google","guides","happen","http","http.","implementation","including","installing","interrupted","interruption","interruptions.","introduced","issue","license.txt","licensed","locally","look","looking","major","may","means","method","mit","modularization","nearly","official","outage.","please","project","provider","re-uploading","reference","remote","resume","resumed","s3-compatible","seamlessly","see","server","servers","sizes","special","specifies","status","storing","support","system","tag","them","tus.github.io","tusd.","under","user","v2.","version","wants","website","which","willingly","without"]},"l